sections: INPUT, OUTPUT, COMMENTS, STAMPS!!
{
	!! FOOP-55: congruent modulo — {a, b, c, 'cmod}$ computes the boolean (a % b == c)
	!! The operator goes INSIDE the brane, exactly as 'mod and 'or do
	!! ({7, 3, 'mod}$). The postfix-juxtaposition form `{a,b,c}'cmod` does NOT
	!! parse — a null-characterized name cannot follow a brane that way
	!! ("expected <token>, found Apostrophe"), which is how this file used to
	!! be written.
	!! NOTE: a comment line that is a BARE separator is not allowed here — the
	!! Foolish einmo suite uses "!!"+newline as its section separator, so an
	!! empty comment line breaks the envelope writer.
	!! 'cmod is NOT YET IMPLEMENTED. FOOP-55 §5 plans it as `congruent_modulo`
	!! defined in pure Foolish rather than as a Rust FIR kind; that route is
	!! currently blocked by D7 (a system operator nested inside a juxtaposed
	!! definition never settles). Until it lands, every row below settles
	!! ECONSTANIC — an unanchored search for a name that is not declared, which
	!! is the correct outcome for a missing operator, NOT a bug in this file.
	r1 = {3, 3, 0, 'cmod}$;    !! 3%3==0 → 'True   (once implemented)
	r2 = {7, 3, 1, 'cmod}$;    !! 7%3==1 → 'True   (once implemented)
	r3 = {7, 3, 0, 'cmod}$;    !! 7%3!=0 → 'False  (once implemented)
}
!!
{WOCONSTANIC
  r1 =$ {WOCONSTANIC (WOCONSTANIC)
      3;
      3;
      0;
      ?(pattern='^'cmod$', UNANCHORED, ECONSTANIC)
  };
  r2 =$ {WOCONSTANIC (WOCONSTANIC)
      7;
      3;
      1;
      ?(pattern='^'cmod$', UNANCHORED, ECONSTANIC)
  };
  r3 =$ {WOCONSTANIC (WOCONSTANIC)
      7;
      3;
      0;
      ?(pattern='^'cmod$', UNANCHORED, ECONSTANIC)
  }
}!!
!!
